  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I worked it out by hand and running the function gave the same number.\n\n1. **Base fee:** `pricing.base_fee(1000)` is `500 + 1000 // 10`, which is 600.\n2. **Discount:** `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: `[REDACTED:PII] * 20) // 100`, which is 480.\n\n`service2` only imports `pricing` and `discounts`. `decoy_tax.py` also has a gold tier (25%), but nothing imports it, so it has no effect. `decoy_shipping.py` isn't used either.\n\nANSWER: 480",
